{
  "sn54.9:0.1": "Linked Discourses 54.9 ",
  "sn54.9:0.2": "1. One Thing ",
  "sn54.9:0.3": "At Vesālī ",
  "sn54.9:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn54.9:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Vesālī, at the Great Wood, in the hall with the peaked roof. ",
  "sn54.9:1.3": "Now at that time the Buddha spoke in many ways to the mendicants about the meditation on ugliness. He praised the meditation on ugliness and its development. ",
  "sn54.9:2.1": "Then the Buddha said to the mendicants, ",
  "sn54.9:2.2": "“Mendicants, I wish to go on retreat for a fortnight. ",
  "sn54.9:2.3": "No-one should approach me, except the one who brings my almsfood.” ",
  "sn54.9:2.4": "“Yes, sir,” replied those mendicants. And no-one approached him, except the one who brought the almsfood. ",
  "sn54.9:3.1": "Then those mendicants thought, ",
  "sn54.9:3.2": "“The Buddha spoke in many ways about the meditation on ugliness. He praised the meditation on ugliness and its development.” They committed themselves to developing the many different facets of the meditation on ugliness. ",
  "sn54.9:3.3": "Becoming horrified, repelled, and disgusted with this body, they looked for a suicide weapon. ",
  "sn54.9:3.4": "Each day ten, twenty, or thirty mendicants committed suicide. ",
  "sn54.9:4.1": "Then after a fortnight had passed, the Buddha came out of retreat and addressed Ānanda, ",
  "sn54.9:4.2": "“Ānanda, why does the mendicant Saṅgha seem so diminished?” ",
  "sn54.9:4.3": "Ānanda told the Buddha all